searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Types.Process","doc":"This module defines process related types used by the MscmpSystUtils library.","ref":"Msutils.Types.Process.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Types.Process.name/0","doc":"The registry qualified name of a process for use in `t:pid/0` lookups.\n\nThis type is compatible with the `t:GenServer.name/0` type with the\naddition of `t:pid/0` as a valid name.","ref":"Msutils.Types.Process.html#t:name/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Types.Process.registry/0","doc":"The registry to use when either looking up a process `t:pid/0` or\nregistering a process's name.\n\nThe currently supported registries are:\n\n* `:local` - The local registry.  Service names must be atoms.\n* `:global` - The global registry.\n* `{module(), term()}` - A registry module and name.  The registry must\n  to usable in `:via` tuple names.  See the `GenServer` documentation\n  regarding name registration for details and requirements.","ref":"Msutils.Types.Process.html#t:registry/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Types.String","doc":"This module defines string related types used by the MscmpSystUtils library.","ref":"Msutils.Types.String.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Types.String.token_sets/0","doc":"","ref":"Msutils.Types.String.html#t:token_sets/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Types.String.tokens/0","doc":"Acceptable token sets for use in generating random strings.","ref":"Msutils.Types.String.html#t:tokens/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Msutils.Types.String.user_defined_tokens/0","doc":"Ad-hoc token set type definition.","ref":"Msutils.Types.String.html#t:user_defined_tokens/0"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils","doc":"This is a set of basic utilities which are generally useful across Components.\n\n<!-- MDESC !-->\n\n> #### `use Msutils.Guards` {: .info}\n>\n> When `use Msutils.Guards` is called, it requires the module and imports the\n> guards it defines into the calling module.","ref":"Msutils.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.String","doc":"This module provides string utilities.","ref":"Msutils.String.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.String.get_random_string/2","doc":"Generates a random string drawn from a specified list of characters.","ref":"Msutils.String.html#get_random_string/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.String.get_random_string/2","doc":"* `string_length` - the number of characters in the returned string.\n\n  * `tokens` - this optional parameter may either be a `charlist()` including\n  the desired characters from which to randomly select characters for the\n  string or the parameter may be an atom which designates a predefined\n  character list.  The available predefined character lists are:\n\n    * `:alphanum` - will return values from the set\n    `0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ`.  This is the default value.\n\n    * `:mixed_alphanum` - will return values from the set\n    `0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz`\n\n    * `b32e` - will return values from the set\n    `0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUV`.  This equates to the character set\n    used by Elixir's `Integer.to_string(x, 32)`.\n\n    * `b32c` - will return values from the set\n    `0123456789ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ`.  This is the Base32 character set\n    compatible with Douglas Crockford's Base 32 (https://www.crockford.com/base32.html).","ref":"Msutils.String.html#get_random_string/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Msutils.String.get_random_string/2","doc":"The following examples demonstrate usage and expected characteristics of the\nfunction.\n\nDefault :alphanum token - 8 characters from 0-9 and A-Z\n\n    iex> result = Msutils.String.get_random_string(8)\n    iex> String.match?(result, ~r/^[0-9A-Z]{8}$/)\n    true\n\nMixed case alphanumeric - 10 characters from 0-9, A-Z, and a-z\n\n    iex> result = Msutils.String.get_random_string(10, :mixed_alphanum)\n    iex> String.match?(result, ~r/^[0-9A-Za-z]{10}$/)\n    true\n\nBase32 Elixir style - 6 characters from 0-9 and A-V\n\n    iex> result = Msutils.String.get_random_string(6, :b32e)\n    iex> String.match?(result, ~r/^[0-9A-V]{6}$/)\n    true\n\nBase32 Crockford style - 6 characters from Crockford's set\n\n    iex> result = Msutils.String.get_random_string(6, :b32c)\n    iex> String.match?(result, ~r/^[0-9ABCDEFGHJKMNPQRSTVWXYZ]{6}$/)\n    true\n\nCustom character list\n\n    iex> result = Msutils.String.get_random_string(4, ~c\"ABC123\")\n    iex> String.match?(result, ~r/^[ABC123]{4}$/)\n    true","ref":"Msutils.String.html#get_random_string/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Process","doc":"This module provides utilities for working with processes.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Process.register/1","doc":"Registers the current process under the given name.\n\nThis function must be called from within the process that is to be registered.\nAttempting to register a process from outside that process will fail.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Process.register/1","doc":"* `name` - The name under which to register the current process.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Process.register/1","doc":"* `:ok` - The process was successfully registered.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :registration_failed}}` -\n    If the registration failed.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :invalid_name}}` -\n    If the provided name does not comply with `t:Msutils.Types.Process.name/0`\n    naming conventions.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Msutils.Process.register/1","doc":"Register a process locally:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register(:my_process)\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:my_process)\n\nRegister a process globally:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register({:global, :my_global_process})\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({:global, :my_global_process})\n\nRegister a process via a registry:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register({:via, Registry, {MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry, :my_process}})\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({:via, Registry, {MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry, :my_process}})\n\nAttempt to register with an already taken name:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid1} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register(:taken_name)\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid1} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:taken_name)\n    iex> {:ok, _} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   {:error, error} = Msutils.Process.register(:taken_name)\n    ...>   %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{kind: :registration, cause: :registration_failed} = error\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Process.register/2","doc":"Registers the current process under the given registry and name.\n\nThis function must be called from within the process that is to be registered.\nAttempting to register a process from outside that process will fail.\n\nThis function provides a convenient way to register processes when the registry and\nname are known separately at runtime.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Process.register/2","doc":"* `registry` - The registry to use for registration.\n  * `name` - The name under which to register the current process.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Process.register/2","doc":"* `:ok` - The process was successfully registered.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :registration_failed}}` -\n    If the registration failed.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :invalid_name}}` -\n    If the provided registry or name combination is invalid.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Msutils.Process.register/2","doc":"Register a process locally:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register(:local, :my_process)\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:local, :my_process)\n\nRegister a process globally:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register(:global, :my_global_process)\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:global, :my_global_process)\n\nRegister a process via a registry:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn ->\n    ...>   Msutils.Process.register({Registry, MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry}, :my_process)\n    ...>   %{}\n    ...> end)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({Registry, MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry}, :my_process)","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#register/2-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Process.whereis/1","doc":"Looks up a process by its name and returns its PID.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Process.whereis/1","doc":"* `name` - The name of the process whose PID is to be retrieved.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/1-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Process.whereis/1","doc":"* `{:ok, pid}` - The PID of the process if found.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :process_not_found}}` -\n    If the process doesn't exist\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :invalid_name}}` -\n    If the provided name does not comply with `t:Msutils.Types.Process.name/0`\n    naming conventions.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/1-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Msutils.Process.whereis/1","doc":"A simple local process name lookup:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: :example_local_name)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:example_local_name)\n\nA global process name lookup:\n\n    iex> {:ok, global_pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: {:global, :example_global_process})\n    iex> {:ok, ^global_pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({:global, :example_global_process})\n\nA via process name lookup:\n    iex> {:ok, via_pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: {:via, Registry, {MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry, :example_via_process}})\n    iex> {:ok, ^via_pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({:via, Registry, {MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry, :example_via_process}})\n\nAttempted lookup of a non-existent process:\n\n    iex> {:error, error} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:nonexistent_process)\n    iex> %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{kind: :lookup, cause: :process_not_found} = error\n\nAttempted lookup of an invalid or unsupported process name:\n\n    iex> {:error, error} = Msutils.Process.whereis({:invalid, :name})\n    iex> %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{kind: :lookup, cause: :invalid_name} = error","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/1-examples"},{"type":"function","title":"Msutils.Process.whereis/2","doc":"Looks up a process by its name and returns its PID.\n\nTypically `whereis/2` is called when neither the registry name (or kind) or\nprocess name are known until runtime.  Since `t:Msutils.Types.Process.name/0`,\nand likewise `t:GenServer.name/0`, values vary in construction based on the\nspecific kind of registry, this function provides a convenient way to not have\nto worry about the name construction.  If the registry kind is known at\ncompile time, then `whereis/1` is preferred as it should be slightly more\nefficient.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Msutils.Process.whereis/2","doc":"* `registry` - The registry to use for the lookup.\n  * `name` - The name of the process whose PID is to be retrieved.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/2-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Msutils.Process.whereis/2","doc":"* `{:ok, pid}` - The PID of the process if found.\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :process_not_found}}` -\n    If the process doesn't exist\n\n  * `{:error, %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{cause: :invalid_name}}` -\n    If the provided name does not comply with `t:Msutils.Types.Process.name/0`\n    naming conventions.","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/2-returns"},{"type":"function","title":"Examples - Msutils.Process.whereis/2","doc":"A simple local process name lookup:\n\n    iex> {:ok, pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: :example2_local_name)\n    iex> {:ok, ^pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:local, :example2_local_name)\n\nA global process name lookup:\n\n    iex> {:ok, global_pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: {:global, :example2_global_process})\n    iex> {:ok, ^global_pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:global, :example2_global_process)\n\nA via process name lookup:\n\n    iex> {:ok, via_pid} = Agent.start_link(fn -> %{} end, name: {:via, Registry, {MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry, :example2_via_process}})\n    iex> {:ok, ^via_pid} = Msutils.Process.whereis({Registry, MscmpSystUtils.TestRegistry}, :example2_via_process)\n\nAttempted lookup of a non-existent process:\n\n    iex> {:error, error} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:local, :nonexistent_process)\n    iex> %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{kind: :lookup, cause: :process_not_found} = error\n\nAttempted lookup of an invalid or unsupported process name:\n\n    iex> {:error, error} = Msutils.Process.whereis(:local, {:invalid, :name})\n    iex> %Mserror.ProcessUtilsError{kind: :lookup, cause: :invalid_name} = error","ref":"Msutils.Process.html#whereis/2-examples"},{"type":"module","title":"Msutils.Guards","doc":"This module defines common guards.","ref":"Msutils.Guards.html"},{"type":"macro","title":"Msutils.Guards.is_reg_atom/1","doc":"A guard function which returns true when the passed value is a regular atom\nthat has no special meaning in Elixir or Erlang.\n\nThis excludes `nil`, `true`, and `false`.","ref":"Msutils.Guards.html#is_reg_atom/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Msutils.Guards.is_reg_atom/1","doc":"iex> is_reg_atom(:an_atom)\n    true\n    iex> is_reg_atom(nil)\n    false\n    iex> is_reg_atom(true)\n    false\n    iex> is_reg_atom(false)\n    false\n    iex> is_reg_atom(\"a string\")\n    false","ref":"Msutils.Guards.html#is_reg_atom/1-examples"},{"type":"macro","title":"Msutils.Guards.is_uuid/1","doc":"Returns `true` when the passed value is a binary string is in a format that\nis consistent with the standard \"8-4-4-4-12\" textual representation of a UUID.\n\n> #### Limitation {: .warning}\n>\n> This guard does not validate that the characters are valid hex digits and thus\n> it will return `true` even in cases where the value is not a valid UUID. In\n> this regard, this guard acts more as a sanity check than a true validation.\n\nFor a more complete check, consider using `Ecto.UUID.dump/1` rather than a\nguard.","ref":"Msutils.Guards.html#is_uuid/1"},{"type":"macro","title":"Examples - Msutils.Guards.is_uuid/1","doc":"Proper UUIDs are validated as expected.\n\n    iex> is_uuid(\"123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000\")\n    true\n\nNon-UUID binaries are rejected.\n\n    iex> is_uuid(\"not a uuid\")\n    false\n\nNon-UUIDs that happen to have the same format of a UUID are also validated.\n\n    iex> is_uuid(\"zzzzzzzz-zzzz-zzzz-zzzz-zzzzzzzzzzzz\")\n    true","ref":"Msutils.Guards.html#is_uuid/1-examples"},{"type":"exception","title":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError","doc":"This module defines the error types for the Msutils.Process module.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html"},{"type":"type","title":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.kinds/0","doc":"Represents the available Kinds of error allowed by this Error type.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#t:kinds/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Available Kinds - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.kinds/0","doc":"* `:lookup` - Indicates that there was an error looking up a process.\n\n  * `:registration` - Indicates that there was an error registering a process.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#t:kinds/0-available-kinds"},{"type":"type","title":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.t/0","doc":"Describes the structure of an error of generated by this exception.\n\nThe `cause` attribute allows for errors to be nested.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"type","title":"Attributes - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.t/0","doc":"The following attributes are those which are set or modified by the\nuser when working with errors.\n\n  * `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#t:t/0-attributes"},{"type":"type","title":"Internal Attributes - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.t/0","doc":"These attributes have their values set at compile time and are used\ninternally by the MscmpSystError framework.  They are not to be altered\nby user code.  Reading these attributes in user code is safe, however.\n\n  * `__mserror__` - Always true, indicates that this error is compatible\n    with the MscmpSystError framework.\n\n  * `__mscomponent__` - The component that generated the error.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#t:t/0-internal-attributes"},{"type":"function","title":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.new/3","doc":"Creates a new error struct with the given kind, message, and options.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#new/3"},{"type":"function","title":"Parameters - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.new/3","doc":"* `kind` - The kind of error, see `t:kinds/0` for the available Kinds.\n\n  * `message` - A string describing the error.\n\n  * `opts` - A keyword list of additional options.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#new/3-parameters"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.new/3","doc":"* `:context` - contextual information for better understanding the\n    error.  If provided, the context should be of type\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.Context.t/0`.\n\n  * `:cause` - The cause of the error, which can be an exception, an error tuple,\n    or any other term.\n\n  * `:parse_error` - An error result conforming with\n    `t:MscmpSystError.Types.parsable_error/0` to be parsed overriding\n    certain attributes of the exception struct.  When provided the\n    `message` parameter is treated as a default message which can be\n    overridden by a message supplied by the error result provided to this\n    option.  The `cause` attribute of the exception struct will be set to\n    a value derived from this option's value, ignoring the `:cause`\n    option if provided; typically you would not provide both\n    `:parse_error` and `:cause` in the same call to `new/3`.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#new/3-options"},{"type":"function","title":"Returns - Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.new/3","doc":"Returns a struct of this error type with the error details.","ref":"Mserror.ProcessUtilsError.html#new/3-returns"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.38.4"}}